From: 14sea <wanhuaning@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 20:02:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Plan=20C-1=20v5=20mode=20H:=20fabric=20surgery?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20SD=20->=20.rbf=20=CF=83=E2=81=BB=C2=B9=20surgery?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20->=20EPCS=20slot=201?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Re-introduces the Phase 8 .rbf-flipping path that was dropped under
Plan C-1 v2 in favor of on-chip TPU LUT memory.  Under v5 we DO touch
fabric configuration: read page-0 .rbf into SDRAM, apply σ⁻¹ XOR per
edits.bin record via lut_apply_with_canon + dirty-frame tracking,
repair frame CRC-16 only on touched frames via
lc_patch_rbf_crc_frames, and program the result to EPCS slot 1.
User then manually copies slot 1 -> slot 0 with openFPGALoader and
power-cycles to load the edited fabric.

First-ship scope is SYMMETRIC MASKS ONLY ({0x0000, 0xFFFF}).  Reason:
Quartus 21.1 Lite silently drops LCCOMB location_assignments
(empirically verified 2026-05-21 against the h1h2 discriminator + the
provider's known-good jbscan), so the original M0-M4 in-iron sentinel
chain can't run.  For symmetric masks the H1 vs H2 distinction is
unobservable (σ permutes identical cells), so codec correctness is
implicitly validated by existing mode g/G silicon evidence.
Asymmetric masks are gated until either Quartus Pro/Standard is
available or a working post-fit placement-query mechanism is found.

Trust chain (unchanged from mode g, plus one new gate):
 - SD NEOLNX magic + layout v4+
 - edits.bin magic + version + n_records + CRC-32 over
   [version|n_records|records]
 - lc_init pin-friendly-column whitelist per record
 - NEW: symmetric-mask whitelist per record (rejects asymmetric
   mask values for first-ship safety)
 - readback SHA-256 byte-identity verify after slot-1 program

Idempotent: re-running mode H with the same edits.bin on the same
page-0 base is a no-op (slot-1 sha matches edited sha → skip write).
Safe to abort at any point: slot 0 (the running bitstream) is never
touched; only slot 1 is.  AS REMOTE is NOT triggered (broken in this
toolchain per [[reference-rublock-complexity]]); promotion is user-
mediated via openFPGALoader.

Build verified (28780 B main.elf, +4.7 KB vs mode-g-only build).
Iron-side untested in this commit; symmetric-mask demo target
(picking a safe LE in production iron to flip 0xFFFF on) is a
follow-up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sw/stage2_loader/main.c | 247 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 247 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sw/stage2_loader/main.c b/sw/stage2_loader/main.c
index 2c0df05..ebe1999 100644
--- a/sw/stage2_loader/main.c
+++ b/sw/stage2_loader/main.c
@@ -35,6 +35,12 @@
  * 10 MB below EDITS_SCRATCH_ADDR.  Fits the same ~368 KB image used as
  * the source, lets us SHA the EPCS contents without clobbering source. */
 #define EPCS_READBACK_ADDR 0x41400000UL
+
+/* Plan C-1 v5 mode H: EP4CE10F17C8 .rbf byte length.  Page 0 and slot 1
+ * are both compiled to exactly this size by Quartus 21.1 Lite under the
+ * project's pinned QSF.  Used by mode_fabric_surgery to bound the SDRAM
+ * scratch buffer + epcs_fast_read length. */
+#define MODE_H_RBF_BYTES   368011u
 #define UART_BAUD         115200
 
 /* Plan C-1 v2: on-chip TPU peripheral at XBUS 0xF0000000.
@@ -2068,6 +2074,245 @@ static void mode_generate_classic(void)
  * Demo intent: after mode_g loads a new edits.bin, mode_c output
  * reflects the loaded data — proving the SD->LUT load actually
  * changes TPU compute behavior, not just stored state. */
+/* mode_fabric_surgery — Plan C-1 v5 mode H: SD-driven σ⁻¹ surgery on the
+ * page-0 .rbf, written to EPCS slot 1 for user-mediated cold-boot
+ * promotion (openFPGALoader slot 1 -> slot 0).  This is the reintroduction
+ * of the Phase 8 .rbf-flipping path that was dropped under C-1 v2 in
+ * favor of on-chip TPU LUT memory; here we DO touch fabric configuration.
+ *
+ * First-ship scope is SYMMETRIC MASKS ONLY ({0x0000, 0xFFFF}).  Reason:
+ * Quartus 21.1 Lite silently drops LCCOMB location_assignments, so the
+ * original M0-M4 in-iron sentinel validation can't run — see
+ * [[feedback-quartus-lite-no-lccomb-lock]] in memory.  For symmetric
+ * masks H1 vs H2 distinction is unobservable (σ permutes identical
+ * cells), so codec correctness is implicitly validated by existing
+ * mode g/G silicon evidence.  Asymmetric masks are gated until the
+ * toolchain limitation is resolved.
+ *
+ * Sequence:
+ *   1. SD boot header (NEOLNX magic + layout v4+).  Same gate as mode_g.
+ *   2. Read edits.bin into SDRAM.
+ *   3. Integrity gate: magic + version + n_records + CRC-32 over
+ *      [version|n_records|records].
+ *   4. Pre-flight reject: mask ∉ {0x0000, 0xFFFF} OR (x,y,n) not in
+ *      pin-friendly whitelist (lc_init dry-run).  Refuse-and-halt
+ *      before touching EPCS.
+ *   5. epcs_fast_read(0, MODE_H_RBF_BYTES) → page 0 .rbf into SDRAM.
+ *   6. For each record: lut_apply_with_canon onto in-SDRAM .rbf +
+ *      lc_mark_dirty into the 216-byte frame bitmap.
+ *   7. lc_patch_rbf_crc_frames(rbf, dirty) — recompute CRC-16 for the
+ *      frames the σ⁻¹ XORs touched (frames 25..1751, dirty subset only).
+ *   8. SHA-256 of edited .rbf → UART log.
+ *   9. Read current slot 1 → SHA-256; if equal to edited, skip write
+ *      (idempotent — running mode H twice with the same edits.bin is
+ *      a no-op).
+ *  10. Else: epcs_write_image(EPCS_TPU_BASE, ...) + readback SHA-256
+ *      verify.  No AS REMOTE — user manually copies slot 1 → slot 0
+ *      via openFPGALoader and power-cycles.  Slot 0 remains safe
+ *      throughout; abortable at any point.
+ */
+static void mode_fabric_surgery(void)
+{
+    uart_puts("[stage2] Mode: fabric surgery (Plan C-1 v5 mode H — "
+              ".rbf σ⁻¹ surgery, EPCS slot 1 staging)\r\n");
+    uart_puts("[rot] first-ship scope: symmetric masks {0x0000, 0xFFFF} "
+              "only; asymmetric gated by [[feedback-quartus-lite-no-lccomb-lock]]\r\n");
+
+    extern int sd_init(void);
+    extern int sd_read_block(uint32_t lba, uint8_t *dst);
+    extern int sd_read_many(uint32_t lba, uint32_t n, uint8_t *dst);
+
+    if (sd_init()) { uart_puts("[sd] init FAIL\r\n"); while (1) {} }
+
+    static uint8_t hdr_buf[512];
+    if (sd_read_block(0, hdr_buf)) {
+        uart_puts("[sd] read hdr FAIL\r\n"); while (1) {}
+    }
+
+    /* Magic + layout version — same gate as mode_g. */
+    const char magic[8] = { 'N','E','O','L','N','X','\0','\0' };
+    for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
+        if (hdr_buf[i] != (uint8_t)magic[i]) {
+            uart_puts("[sd] bad magic\r\n"); while (1) {}
+        }
+    }
+    struct sd_boot_hdr *h = (struct sd_boot_hdr *)hdr_buf;
+    if (h->layout_version < 4) {
+        uart_puts("[!] layout_version="); uart_puthex32(h->layout_version);
+        uart_puts(" < 4 — re-pack SD with sd_pack.py to get edits.bin slot\r\n");
+        while (1) {}
+    }
+    if (h->edits_sz == 0) {
+        uart_puts("[!] header edits_sz=0 — SD packed without --edits;"
+                  " re-pack with host/gen_edits_h.py output\r\n");
+        while (1) {}
+    }
+    if (h->edits_sz < sizeof(struct edits_hdr)) {
+        uart_puts("[!] edits_sz="); uart_puthex32(h->edits_sz);
+        uart_puts(" < edits_hdr — corrupt header field\r\n");
+        while (1) {}
+    }
+
+    uart_puts("[sd] edits_lba=");  uart_puthex32(h->edits_lba);
+    uart_puts(" edits_sz=");       uart_puthex32(h->edits_sz);
+    uart_puts("\r\n");
+
+    /* === Step 2: read edits.bin into SDRAM === */
+    uint32_t edits_blks = (h->edits_sz + 511) / 512;
+    uart_puts("[sd] reading edits.bin\r\n");
+    if (sd_read_many(h->edits_lba, edits_blks,
+                     (uint8_t *)EDITS_SCRATCH_ADDR)) {
+        uart_puts("[!] SD read FAIL lba="); uart_puthex32(h->edits_lba);
+        uart_puts("\r\n"); while (1) {}
+    }
+
+    /* === Step 3: integrity gate on edits.bin (magic + version + CRC-32). */
+    const struct edits_hdr *eh =
+        (const struct edits_hdr *)EDITS_SCRATCH_ADDR;
+    if (eh->magic != EDITS_MAGIC) {
+        uart_puts("[!] edits.bin bad magic="); uart_puthex32(eh->magic);
+        uart_puts("\r\n"); while (1) {}
+    }
+    if (eh->version != EDITS_VERSION) {
+        uart_puts("[!] edits.bin version="); uart_puthex32(eh->version);
+        uart_puts(" unsupported\r\n"); while (1) {}
+    }
+    uint32_t need = sizeof(struct edits_hdr)
+                  + (uint32_t)eh->n_records * sizeof(struct edit_rec);
+    if (need > h->edits_sz) {
+        uart_puts("[!] edits.bin truncated\r\n"); while (1) {}
+    }
+    const uint8_t *eb = (const uint8_t *)EDITS_SCRATCH_ADDR;
+    uint32_t records_bytes = (uint32_t)eh->n_records
+                           * (uint32_t)sizeof(struct edit_rec);
+    uint32_t got_crc = crc32_two(eb + 4, 8,
+                                 eb + sizeof(struct edits_hdr),
+                                 records_bytes);
+    if (got_crc != eh->crc32) {
+        uart_puts("[!] edits.bin CRC FAIL computed=");
+        uart_puthex32(got_crc); uart_puts(" expected=");
+        uart_puthex32(eh->crc32); uart_puts("\r\n");
+        while (1) {}
+    }
+    uart_puts("[rot] edits.bin CRC OK n_records=");
+    uart_puthex32(eh->n_records); uart_puts("\r\n");
+
+    /* === Step 4: pre-flight — symmetric-mask gate + pin-friendly gate.
+     * Done BEFORE reading page-0 .rbf so we fail fast on bad records and
+     * never half-write EPCS.  lut_apply_with_canon also re-checks
+     * lc_init internally; the redundancy is intentional. */
+    const struct edit_rec *recs =
+        (const struct edit_rec *)((const uint8_t *)EDITS_SCRATCH_ADDR
+                                  + sizeof(struct edits_hdr));
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < eh->n_records; i++) {
+        if (recs[i].mask != 0x0000u && recs[i].mask != 0xFFFFu) {
+            uart_puts("[!] edit#"); uart_puthex32(i);
+            uart_puts(" mask="); uart_puthex32(recs[i].mask);
+            uart_puts(" rejected — mode H first-ship accepts only "
+                      "symmetric masks {0x0000, 0xFFFF}\r\n");
+            while (1) {}
+        }
+        lut_codec_t lc;
+        lc_status_t st = lc_init(&lc, recs[i].x, recs[i].y, recs[i].n);
+        if (st != LC_OK) {
+            uart_puts("[!] edit#"); uart_puthex32(i);
+            uart_puts(" (x="); uart_puthex32(recs[i].x);
+            uart_puts(",y="); uart_puthex32(recs[i].y);
+            uart_puts(",n="); uart_puthex32(recs[i].n);
+            uart_puts(") rejected by lc_init status=");
+            uart_puthex32((uint32_t)st); uart_puts("\r\n");
+            while (1) {}
+        }
+    }
+    uart_puts("[rot] pre-flight OK: ");
+    uart_puthex32(eh->n_records);
+    uart_puts(" records pass symmetric-mask + pin-friendly gates\r\n");
+
+    /* === Step 5: read page-0 .rbf from EPCS into SDRAM. === */
+    uint8_t *rbf = (uint8_t *)TPU_SCRATCH_ADDR;
+    uart_puts("[rot] reading page-0 .rbf ("); uart_puthex32(MODE_H_RBF_BYTES);
+    uart_puts(" B) from EPCS -> SDRAM @"); uart_puthex32(TPU_SCRATCH_ADDR);
+    uart_puts("\r\n");
+    epcs_fast_read(0u, MODE_H_RBF_BYTES, rbf);
+
+    /* === Step 6: σ⁻¹ XOR onto in-SDRAM .rbf + dirty-frame tracking. */
+    static uint8_t dirty[CRC_DIRTY_BITMAP_BYTES];
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < CRC_DIRTY_BITMAP_BYTES; i++) dirty[i] = 0;
+
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < eh->n_records; i++) {
+        lc_status_t st = lut_apply_with_canon(rbf,
+                                              recs[i].x, recs[i].y, recs[i].n,
+                                              recs[i].mask, dirty);
+        if (st != LC_OK) {
+            /* Should be unreachable — pre-flight already passed lc_init. */
+            uart_puts("[!] edit#"); uart_puthex32(i);
+            uart_puts(" lut_apply_with_canon FAIL status=");
+            uart_puthex32((uint32_t)st); uart_puts("\r\n");
+            while (1) {}
+        }
+    }
+    uart_puts("[rot] σ⁻¹ XOR applied to "); uart_puthex32(eh->n_records);
+    uart_puts(" record(s) in SDRAM\r\n");
+
+    /* === Step 7: per-frame CRC-16 repair on touched frames only. */
+    lc_patch_rbf_crc_frames(rbf, dirty);
+    uart_puts("[rot] frame CRC-16 repair complete (dirty-frame walk)\r\n");
+
+    /* === Step 8: SHA-256 of edited .rbf for the log. === */
+    uint32_t H_new[8];
+    sha256_hw(rbf, MODE_H_RBF_BYTES, H_new);
+    uart_puts("[rot] edited .rbf sha256=");
+    for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) uart_puthex32(H_new[i]);
+    uart_puts("\r\n");
+
+    /* === Step 9: idempotency — read slot 1, SHA-compare, skip write
+     * if it's already what we'd be about to write. */
+    uint8_t *rb = (uint8_t *)EPCS_READBACK_ADDR;
+    uint32_t H_slot1[8];
+    uart_puts("[rot] reading EPCS slot 1 @"); uart_puthex32(EPCS_TPU_BASE);
+    uart_puts(" for idempotency check\r\n");
+    epcs_fast_read(EPCS_TPU_BASE, MODE_H_RBF_BYTES, rb);
+    sha256_hw(rb, MODE_H_RBF_BYTES, H_slot1);
+    uart_puts("[rot] slot 1 sha256=");
+    for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) uart_puthex32(H_slot1[i]);
+    uart_puts("\r\n");
+    int already = 1;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) if (H_slot1[i] != H_new[i]) { already = 0; break; }
+
+    if (already) {
+        uart_puts("[rot] slot 1 already byte-identical to edited .rbf "
+                  "— skipping EPCS write (idempotent)\r\n");
+    } else {
+        /* === Step 10: epcs_write_image + readback SHA verify. === */
+        uart_puts("[rot] writing edited .rbf to EPCS slot 1\r\n");
+        int rc = epcs_write_image(EPCS_TPU_BASE, rbf, MODE_H_RBF_BYTES);
+        if (rc != 0) {
+            uart_puts("[!] epcs_write_image FAIL rc=");
+            uart_puthex32((uint32_t)rc); uart_puts("\r\n");
+            while (1) {}
+        }
+        epcs_fast_read(EPCS_TPU_BASE, MODE_H_RBF_BYTES, rb);
+        sha256_hw(rb, MODE_H_RBF_BYTES, H_slot1);
+        for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
+            if (H_slot1[i] != H_new[i]) {
+                uart_puts("[!] readback SHA FAIL — slot 1 != edited "
+                          ".rbf at word "); uart_puthex32((uint32_t)i);
+                uart_puts(" got="); uart_puthex32(H_slot1[i]);
+                uart_puts(" exp="); uart_puthex32(H_new[i]);
+                uart_puts("\r\n"); while (1) {}
+            }
+        }
+        uart_puts("[rot] EPCS slot 1 readback SHA OK ("
+                  "byte-identical to edited .rbf)\r\n");
+    }
+
+    uart_puts("[rot] mode H complete — slot 1 staged with σ⁻¹ fabric edits.\r\n");
+    uart_puts("[rot] user action required: openFPGALoader copy slot 1 "
+              "(0x80000) -> slot 0 (0x00000), then power-cycle to load "
+              "edited fabric.  Slot 0 unchanged until user promotes; "
+              "safe to abort at this point with no fabric change.\r\n");
+}
+
 static void mode_compute(void)
 {
     uart_puts("[stage2] Mode: TPU compute (Plan C-1 v3 — LUT-driven)\r\n");
@@ -2274,6 +2519,8 @@ int main(void)
             mode_generate();           /* Plan C-1 v2: SD→LUT loader (raw mask) */
         } else if (mode == 'G') {
             mode_generate_classic();   /* Plan C-1 v4: SD→LUT loader with σ⁻¹ math */
+        } else if (mode == 'H') {
+            mode_fabric_surgery();     /* Plan C-1 v5: SD→.rbf σ⁻¹ surgery→EPCS slot 1 */
         } else if (mode == 'c') {
             mode_compute();            /* Plan C-1 v3: LUT-driven TPU compute demo */
         } else if (mode == 'P') {
